 Nexus  Overview ▾  1/6                       ● Unavailable
╭ Set up NetworkManager ───────────────────────────────────╮
│ ● NetworkManager is not running                          │
│ Nexus manages networks through NetworkManager and it is  │
│ not answering on the system bus, although it is          │
│ installed.                                               │
│                                                          │
│ ● systemd-networkd is also managing your network         │
│                                                          │
│ Switch off what manages your network now, then start     │
│ NetworkManager. The steps are in order.                  │
│   $ sudo systemctl disable --now                         │
│ systemd-networkd.service                                 │
│   $ sudo systemctl enable --now NetworkManager.service   │
│                                                          │
│ Press f to run these steps for you. Administrator steps  │
│ ask for your password first.                             │
│                                                          │
╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯
 f fix  h/l tab  : palette  ? help  q quit
